#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:26
msgid "**Types make code faster.** The bytecode is typed, generics monomorphize, and primitive buffers stay flat: a fixed array of `f32` is a packed `f32` buffer, not an array of boxed numbers. There is no JIT and none is needed â the code shape a JS JIT exists to speculate on (polymorphic property loads) does not exist in rut."
