#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:44
msgid "**Reference counting; no collector.** Objects die the moment their last reference goes away, so destructors are deterministic â host resources (threads, sockets, textures) release at a knowable point, not \"sometime at GC\". Strong cycles leak by design; weak references are the first-class answer. See [memory](memory.md)."
