#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:80
msgid "**Too slow without a JIT.** Interpreter-only JS runs one to two orders of magnitude slower, because a JS engine's speed _is_ its JIT. rut's no-JIT stance is viable only because the language is statically typed: calls bind statically whenever the call site names one concrete type, and dynamic dispatch is a checked vtable hop that happens only where the program actually erases types."
